    "body": "Hello Mark,\n\nOur price for Unit 1 Eleanor Trade Centre went over yesterday afternoon and your out-of-office came back straight away, so I am re-sending it - along with our terms and conditions, which the proposal refers to and did not carry.\n\nThe price is GBP 7,975.85 for the four aluminium windows and the door to the ground floor.\n\nOne question while I have you. We priced this same unit for you in April on a different scope - six uPVC windows over both floors, at GBP 4,252.16 - and we never heard back. I am not asking you to revisit it. I would just like to know what happened, because we quote for Bradford Watts often and I would rather understand what we are getting wrong than keep sending prices into the same silence.\n\n",
    "evidence": "July: issued 28/07/2026 14:22 from estimating@, GBP 7,975.85; out-of-office received 14:23. April: quoted to Mark Golden 20/04/2026 16:23, revised 16:38, GBP 4,252.16 for six uPVC windows - Mary has the file. Both figures are ex VAT and both come from messages that left the building. The scope difference is hers too: April both floors in uPVC, July ground floor in aluminium plus a door.",
